                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55abb646-4b06-3824-bbcf-b4ec6be18a47",
                                        "entry_id": "729332ce-3052-3356-b0f9-c9b203bc75f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An exaggerated use of the sound of the letter R."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29fca372-757f-3086-8910-90400519e9a3",
                                        "entry_id": "729332ce-3052-3356-b0f9-c9b203bc75f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A linguistic phenomenon in which a consonant changes into an R; rhotacization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edc3645e-e0bb-3830-a02e-c69a98c37cfb",
                                        "entry_id": "729332ce-3052-3356-b0f9-c9b203bc75f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The inability to pronounce the letter R; derhotacization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a30047b-ddda-47a5-ab80-a894f320ee9b",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3645e-e0bb-3830-a02e-c69a98c37cfb",
                                                "text": "For example: r’s may become burrs or guttural grunts or w’s or l’s (rhotacism); […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c389c620-c553-435e-b800-bd62b8f3fdcf",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3645e-e0bb-3830-a02e-c69a98c37cfb",
                                                "text": "From the analysis of Kana writings, hypothesizes that the inability to establish a stable… […] The correction of rhotacism by means of an electric vibrator."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7987e40e-a1ac-4931-8925-93bfaaad79de",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3645e-e0bb-3830-a02e-c69a98c37cfb",
                                                "text": "It is universally accepted that the rhotacism, a defective utterance of the /r/ sounds, is usually the last and most difficult American English consonant to correct functionally.\nI use two methods to help correct the rhotacism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fb0adf46-f457-4972-91e3-cf54feb69a0e",
                        "source_entry_id": "a54a6944-f64f-3953-9769-e122bc794199",
                        "source_sense_id": "a98c8222-dddc-36dc-af62-b9adc1a6d910",
